      {
        "name": "stopTrigger",
        "type": {
          "kind": "name",
          "name": "trigger"
        },
        "access": "public",
        "default": "Stop",
        "hidden": false,
        "attribute": {
          "group": "One-shots",
          "tooltip": "Attacks, rolls and reactions are played by TRIGGER, by name (`_playTrigger`): the animator has a state each one enters, which leaves on its own at the clip's end. The graph owns every clip, its speed and its blends; the script owns the gameplay, and asks the animator how long what a trigger plays lasts (`Animator.triggerInfo`) and whether it still plays (`Animator.activeTrigger`). These two take the one-shot's layer back to rest from anything: with its blend-out, and at once."
        }
      },
